IOP native code: a module of more than 8 chunks (512 instructions each) is written as part files of 8 chunks (iopn_<module>_p<k>.cpp, external chunk names) plus its main file with the chunk table and the dispatcher, so the parts compile in parallel. The generated code of every chunk is unchanged (a chunk only jumps inside itself); stale part files of a module are removed. 989nomid (59 chunks, 10.8 MB of C++) was one unit of 126.5 s, the longest of the game build and of the native rebuild after the first-play recording; split into 8 parts the longest takes 24.5 s (Xeon E5-2666 v3, clang -O3 + PGO). Game boots, plays and its sound driver runs natively.

